%% 04b-auth-user-read.mmd - Authentication and authorization: user login and jurisdiction-scoped read
%% Basis: BRIEF §2, §5 (jurisdiction-scoped reads); WP §12.2 (bearer token with scopes), §9; LEC S7 (403 for another jurisdiction)
%% SUPERSEDED 2026-09-26: Scope rules, collection narrowing and parent-record visibility are PROPOSALS.
%% Decisions: my-decisions §10. JWT + POST /login confirmed by you. Scope rules, collection narrowing and
%% parent-record visibility are DECIDED (2026-09-26). Own JWT, NOT a full OAuth flow.
%% SUPERSEDED 2026-09-26: the load-then-404-then-403 order below (scoped users now get 403 before 404; national users 404).
%% SUPERSEDED 2026-09-26: an explicit filter naming another jurisdiction gives 403 (now 200 with count 0).
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant U as User
  participant A as API
  participant DB as MongoDB
  U->>A: POST /solar/v1.0/login with username and password (devices use installation_id and device_key, diagram 04a)
  A->>DB: find user and compare bcrypt hash
  alt credentials not accepted
    A-->>U: 401 + WWW-Authenticate Bearer realm solar + error body
  else accepted
    A-->>U: 200 + signed JWT (scope, jurisdiction_level, jurisdiction_id, short expiry)
  end
  U->>A: GET /solar/v1.0/installations/{installation-id} with Authorization Bearer JWT
  alt token missing, invalid or expired
    A-->>U: 401 + WWW-Authenticate
  else token lacks scope solar:read (for example a device token)
    A-->>U: 403 (40303) + WWW-Authenticate error insufficient_scope
  else token valid
    A->>DB: load installation inside the token jurisdiction (its stored district and province ids; national: no limit)
    alt found
      A-->>U: 200 or 304
    else not found, province or district user
      A-->>U: 403 (40301), whether or not the id exists (403 before 404)
    else not found, national user
      A-->>U: 404 (40402)
    end
  end
  Note over U,A: Collections are narrowed to the caller scope. An explicit filter naming another jurisdiction gives 200 with count 0, not 403 (DECIDED)
  Note over U,A: Readings under a substation, district or province: the scope check runs on the PATH PARENT (OQ-04). A province route is broader than a district user, so 403
  Note over U,A: User tokens never carry readings:write, so POST readings gives 403 (40303). Scope installations:write (admin, national) is only for installation POST, PUT, DELETE (OQ-03 decided)
